\ test.h2o: expect assertions and a test runner over catch/throw. A passing
\ expect is silent; test prints ok <name> or FAIL <name>: <reason>, tallies it,
\ and continues past a failure; test-report prints the count and throws on any
\ failure (so a program-file run exits nonzero — caught here to show the line).

\ === passing assertions: expect=, expect-near, expect (truthy), expect-throws ===
"eq" [: 2 3 + 5 expect= :] test
"near" [: 10 3 / 3.3333 0.01 expect-near :] test
"truthy" [: 2 3 < expect :] test
"throws" [: [: "boom" throw :] expect-throws :] test

\ === failures: the message names expected vs actual; a runtime error's :message is the reason ===
"eq fails" [: 2 2 + 5 expect= :] test
"truthy fails" [: 1 2 > expect :] test
"a runtime error becomes the reason" [: { :a 1 } :missing @ :] test

\ === test-report tallies and throws on any failure ===
[: test-report :] [: drop :] try-catch
